/**
 * One followable direction within a {@link RouteLeg}, e.g. "Turn right at 3110,
 * then walk 12 m" or "3335 (Class Room 3335) is on your left".
 *
 * Plain value type with no identity, returned inside {@link RouteLeg#steps}.
 * Steps are computed server-side from the same graph edges that price the leg,
 * so the {@link RouteStep#meters} of a leg's steps add up to
 * {@link RouteLeg#meters}.
 *
 * ### Kinds
 *
 * {@link RouteStep#kind} is one of five values:
 *
 * - `start` — first step of the first leg: where you begin and how far to walk.
 * - `straight` — first walk after a `connector` step, before any turn.
 * - `turn` — a bearing change of more than 30 degrees: "Turn left", "Turn
 *   right", or (over 150 degrees) "Turn around", optionally naming a room or
 *   connector at the turn, then the distance to the next step.
 * - `connector` — first step of every later leg: "Take West Stairs up to
 *   Level 3". Zero meters and seconds; the ride time is part of
 *   {@link NavRoute#totalSeconds}, not of the leg.
 * - `arrive` — last step of the last leg, saying which side the destination is
 *   on ("3335 is on your left at Elevator C (east)"). When the last hop bends
 *   off the hallway into the room, the arrive step carries that hop's meters
 *   and seconds; otherwise zero.
 */
type RouteStep {

  /**
   * One of `start`, `straight`, `turn`, `connector`, `arrive` (see the
   * type-level note).
   */
  kind: !string

  /**
   * The direction phrased for a student, ready to display verbatim.
   */
  text: !string

  /**
   * Distance walked during this step, in meters, from the authored
   * {@link NavEdge#meters} of the hops it covers.
   */
  meters: !double

  /**
   * Walking time for this step, in seconds, from the authored
   * {@link NavEdge#seconds} of the hops it covers.
   */
  seconds: !double

  /**
   * Index into the leg's {@link RouteLeg#points} of the point where this step
   * begins, so the UI can highlight it on the map.
   */
  pointIndex: !int
}
